text":{"lede":"Yesterday's high of 13\u00b0F was typical for November 13.","t_yest":"November 13: a typical high, but a warm night","p_yest":"The high of <strong>13\u00b0F</strong> was typical for November 13. The normal high for the date is 13\u00b0F, and the record is 35\u00b0F (2014). The low of <strong>12\u00b0F</strong> was the 10th warmest November 13 low (tied) of 107 since 1920.","t_rec":"Record highs keep coming. Record lows have nearly stopped.","p_rec":"If Utqiagvik (Barrow)'s climate weren't changing, every year would have the same chance of holding a daily record. Since 2000, Utqiagvik (Barrow) has set <strong class=\"sig\">15 standing record lows</strong>, far fewer than the 92 that chance alone would give, and <strong class=\"sig\">146 record highs</strong>, far more than the 93 that chance alone would give. The 2010s hold the most record highs of any decade (66). Utqiagvik (Barrow)'s all-time high is 79\u00b0F, on July 13, 1993.","t_chg":"Utqiagvik (Barrow) has warmed, days and nights alike","p_chg":"Across 102 complete years: Utqiagvik (Barrow)'s average low has risen <strong class='sig'>+0.69\u00b0F per decade</strong> (95% range +0.53 to +0.85), about +7.2\u00b0F since 1921. Utqiagvik (Barrow)'s average high has risen <strong class='sig'>+0.56\u00b0F per decade</strong> (95% range +0.39 to +0.74), about +5.9\u00b0F since 1921.","t_mon":"Lows rose in all 12 months. Highs rose in 11 of 12 months.","t_rain":"Utqiagvik (Barrow) has gotten wetter","p_rain":"Utqiagvik (Barrow)'s yearly precipitation has risen <strong class='sig'>+0.24 inches per decade</strong> (95% range +0.13 to +0.36), about +2.5 inches since 1921. The 1991\u20132020 normal is 5.3 inches a year. The wettest year was 2019 (10.11 in); the driest, 1934 (1.00 in).","show_snow":true,"sig_bars":{"lo":true,"hi":true},"t_year":"2026 so far: 7 daily record highs, 2 daily record lows"}}